By Cernunnos, I am a true man, not a bloody courtier!	以 Cernunnos 之名起誓，我是個道地的漢子，不是什麼該死的朝臣！
I may be a loyal servant, but if you dare to insult me in such a fashion, you may find an intimate portion of yourself skinned and hung to dry!	我雖是忠心的僕從，但你若膽敢如此羞辱於我，小心自己身上某個隱私部位被剝了皮、掛起來風乾！
There is no room in your pack.  The Hunter has sworn to deliver them to Camelot and that is good enough.	你的行囊已無空間。獵人已立誓將它們送至肯萊特，這樣便已足夠。
They do not belong to you.	此物並非你所有。
But, m'lord, you already have the spear.	但，吾王，長槍已在你手中。
You are the king, Arthur, not some common bandit. The Hunter seems a reasonable man.  Obtain the spear in a manner that befits you.	你是國王，亞瑟，不是什麼尋常的盜賊。這獵人看來是個通情達理之人。你當以合乎身分的方式取得那把長槍。
What rubbish is this? You are a king.  Behave like one.	這是什麼胡言亂語？你是一國之君，該有一國之君的樣子。
I gave my last bit of tin to Widdershins.	我把最後一點錫器都給了 Widdershins。
My racks are but a few branches notched together. Nothing of worth to you, m'lord.	我這些架子不過是幾根刻了痕的樹枝拼湊而成，於吾王而言不值一提。
As you have guessed, I do carry a knife for hunting and skinning, but I could not part with it and still practice my trade.	如你所料，我確實隨身帶著一把獵刀，用來剝皮宰殺，但少了它，我這行當便做不下去了，恕難割愛。
They are yours, m'lord.  I will deliver them to Camelot for you, by my oath as your loyal man.	它們是吾王的了。我以忠僕之名立誓，會替你把它們送到肯萊特。
You have generously given me the price of the skins already, m'lord.  Consider them yours.	吾王已慷慨付清了這些獸皮的價錢，就當它們是你的吧。
Since your mission is clearly urgent, I give you my oath of honor to deliver them safely to Camelot for you.	既然你的使命顯然十萬火急，我便以名譽立誓，會安全地替你送到肯萊特。
I would be happy to sell them to you, m'lord, for but a single silver coin.	吾王若肯出一枚銀幣，我很樂意割愛。
You have been more than generous to me.  Allow me to give the spear to you.	你待我已是仁至義盡，容我將這把長槍奉上。
I would sell this spear to no other man save you, m'lord.  Forgive my audacity, but the spear is of such value, I could not part with it for less than the price of a gold coin.	這把長槍，除了吾王，我誰也不賣。恕我斗膽直言，此槍價值不菲，若非一枚金幣，我實難割捨。
But sire, you have not asked to buy anything from me.	但陛下，您還沒開口向我買什麼東西呢。
Your entire purse, m'lord? I could not!  I am not a greedy man, only a needy one.	吾王的整個錢囊？這萬萬使不得！我並非貪婪之人，只是手頭拮据罷了。
I am not a man of war.  Such things are not for me.	我不是個好戰之人，這些東西與我無緣。
I would not dare to even lay hands upon it!	我連碰都不敢碰它！
I beg your pardon, sire, but I see no horse.	恕我直言，陛下，我沒見著什麼馬。
A noble offer!  Yet as a poor man, I could never afford to care for such a huge beast.	好慷慨的提議！只是我不過一介窮人，實在養不起這麼大的牲畜。
I have never been fond of mules since I was badly bitten by one.  I beg you to keep it.	自從被一頭騾子狠狠咬過之後，我便對牠們無甚好感。還請你自己留著吧。
Even if you find the mule, what use would I have for a creature that would run away when I enter the Forest?	就算找回那頭騾子，牠一進森林便要逃竄，我留著又有何用？
Without a horse, m'lord, such things are of no use to me.	沒有馬，吾王，這些東西對我毫無用處。
Your generosity is a credit to your name, but you will need it more than I.	你的慷慨足以為你的名聲增光，但你比我更需要這個。
Tis a lovely thing, but of no use to me.	這東西是挺可愛，只是對我沒什麼用處。
I have heard of such wondrous things, but I will not touch it, thank you all the same.	我聽聞過這等奇物，但還是不碰為妙，多謝美意。
Nay, pardon me, but I shall not touch this lady's sleeve.  It belongs to a man who died for her love at the hands of the Black Knight and I would not disturb his ghost.	不，恕我不能碰這條夫人的絲巾。它屬於一位為她的愛情、死於黑武士之手的男子，我不願驚擾他的亡魂。
Nay, m'lord.  It is yours now.  May it serve you well.	不必了，吾王。這如今是你的了，願它能為你所用。
My racks are naught but a few branches notched together.  Nothing of worth to you, m'lord.	我這些架子不過是幾根刻了痕的樹枝拼湊而成，於吾王而言不值一提。
Though I love to barter as much as the next man, I sense that your mission is important and you are anxious to ride on.	雖說我和誰都愛討價還價，但我看得出你的使命重大，急著上路。
The price of a silver coin is all I ask.	我只求一枚銀幣的價錢。
I am open to offers, m'lord, if you can but make them clear to my simple mind.	吾王若有意出價，儘管明說，我這粗淺的腦子自會明白。
Why, m'lord?	為何，吾王？
For what, m'lord?	所為何事，吾王？
Thank you, m'lord!  And by my word as your loyal man, I will deliver them personally to Camelot.	多謝吾王！我以忠僕之名立誓，必親自將它們送到肯萊特。
With all respect, sire, this is not quite enough.	恕我直言，陛下，這還不太夠。
Bless you, m'lord!  I will fetch the spear.	願神保佑吾王！我這就去取長槍來。
I--I am nearly speechless at such a gift!  A thousand blessings upon you!  My family and I will pray for you every night and light candles in your name at church.	我——這樣的厚禮，教我幾乎說不出話來！千萬個祝福都不足以回報你！我全家將每夜為你祈禱，並在教堂為你點上蠟燭。
Bless you, m'lord, bless you!  I shall sing your praises to every man I meet!	願神保佑吾王，保佑吾王！我逢人便要傳頌你的美名！
May Cernunnos, God of the Hunt, bless you!  If there is any advice I may give you, you have but to ask.  And heed this warning: beware the Mad Monk of Glastonbury!	願狩獵之神 Cernunnos 保佑吾王！若有什麼建言，只管開口便是。還有一句忠告，請務必謹記：小心格列斯登伯利的瘋僧侶！
Listen! There is a rustling in the bushes. Something heavy approaches.	聽！灌木叢裡傳來窸窣聲，有什麼沉重的東西正在靠近。
The spear has sunk deeply into the carcass. Your final blow was your most powerful.	長槍深深沒入了屍體。你這最後一擊，是全程中最有力的一下。
Where there is decay, there will be flies.	有腐敗之處，必有蒼蠅聚集。
Sorrow not over the death of these savage creatures. They would just as readily have gutted you.	不必為這些凶殘野獸的死而傷懷，牠們同樣會毫不猶豫地開膛破你的肚腹。
Continue your search.	繼續你的搜尋。
There is the inevitable aftermath of battle -- blood and death.	這是戰鬥過後在所難免的景象——鮮血與死亡。
You fought well, but it is not a pretty sight.	你這一戰打得漂亮，但眼前的景象卻不忍卒睹。
It has sunk deeply into the carcass. Your final blow was your most powerful.	它深深沒入了屍體。你這最後一擊，是全程中最有力的一下。
There is plenty of it.	這東西多得是。
Boars have deadly tusks and an evil temperament to match.	野豬有致命的獠牙，脾性也同樣兇惡。
Ridiculous.	荒謬。
Forget the spear. It will serve you no more.	別管那把長槍了，它再也派不上用場。
The battle is over.	戰鬥已經結束。
The boars are dead. What would that accomplish?	野豬已經死了，這麼做又有何意義？
It is too firmly wedged inside the boar. You must leave it there, I fear.	它牢牢卡在野豬的屍身裡，恐怕你只能就此放棄了。
That would be a long, tedious and bloody job. Your mission is urgent. Leave the spear as it is.	那將是一件冗長、繁瑣又血腥的工作。你的使命緊急，就讓長槍留在原處吧。
Although the flesh of the wild pig is delicious, it would take much time and effort which you do not have to spare.	野豬肉雖然美味，但處理起來費時費力，你並沒有多餘的時間。
Your humor leaves much to be desired.	你這玩笑開得，實在不怎麼高明。
How unsavory. Even the followers of Mithras no longer practice this. Now they drink wine instead of blood in their resurrection rituals. The Christians have followed this tradition as well.	真是令人作嘔。就連米夏拉的信徒如今都已不再這麼做，他們在復活儀式中改以酒代血，基督徒也沿襲了這個作法。
Your ferocious battle has driven any other boars away, luckily for you.	你這場凶猛的搏鬥，已把其餘的野豬都嚇跑了，算你走運。
That would be boring.	那未免太乏味了。
The normal sounds of the forest have returned, along with the buzzing of the flies.	森林恢復了尋常的聲響，還夾雜著蒼蠅的嗡嗡聲。
All is deathly silent in the aftermath of this struggle.	這場搏鬥過後，四下一片死寂。
The strong, foul odor of the boars overwhelms all else.	野豬身上濃烈的惡臭，蓋過了一切其他氣味。
You cannot help such creatures. The giant boars of the Forest Perilous live only to kill.	這種生物你幫不了。派瑞樂斯森林裡的巨型野豬，生來便只為殺戮。
If this were a hunt, perhaps it would be worth the toil, but you are on a sacred mission. It is time to move on.	若這只是一場狩獵，或許值得如此費力，但你身負神聖的使命，該是啟程的時候了。
Mighty as Excaliber is, it is not long enough to kill the boar before it can reach you.	聖劍雖然威力強大，卻不夠長，來不及在野豬撲到你身前將牠擊殺。
Listen! There is a rustling in the bushes.  Something heavy approaches.	聽！灌木叢裡傳來窸窣聲，有什麼沉重的東西正在靠近。
The boars have trampled the ground here keeping it clear of the thick undergrowth which borders it.	野豬在此地踐踏出一片空地，四周濃密的灌木叢因而不得侵入。
The boar has gored you to the core. Alas, King Arthur is no more.	野豬的獠牙深深刺穿了你的要害。唉，亞瑟王，就此殞落。
That is one crow we can do without.	少了這隻烏鴉，倒也無妨。
Heed the words of the crow, for it is no ordinary bird.  It is the voice of the Black Knight.	留意這烏鴉所言，牠並非尋常飛禽，而是黑武士的化聲。
'Tis a Father Tree.  Sometimes, if you are worthy enough, such wise and ancient beings will even speak with you.	這便是老父樹。有時，若你夠格，這等睿智的古老生靈甚至願意開口與你交談。
Clearly, he was once a stout knight.  Naught is left but a bit of armour, his bones picked clean by the crow.	顯然，他生前曾是位健壯的騎士。如今只剩下幾片盔甲，骨頭早被烏鴉啄得乾乾淨淨。
Clearly, he was once a stout knight.  Naught is left but a bit of armour, his bones picked clean by the crow, and a bit of brightly colored silk.	顯然，他生前曾是位健壯的騎士。如今只剩下幾片盔甲、被烏鴉啄得乾乾淨淨的骨頭，還有一小片色彩鮮豔的絲巾。
The rock juts from the heart of the forest like a jagged tooth.  There is evil power within it.	這塊岩石從森林深處突出，宛如一顆參差的獠牙，其中蘊藏著邪惡的力量。
These mushrooms are of the species Amanita Muscaria. They are very dangerous at the best of times, and said to cause madness or death.	這些蕈菇屬於毒蠅傘一類，即便在最尋常的情況下也極為危險，據說會致人瘋狂或死亡。
The clearing is as you left it, but now, to your everlasting shame, this poor soul is no longer the only dead knight in the forest.	這片空地一如你離去時的模樣，但如今，令你永生蒙羞的是，這可憐的亡魂已不再是森林裡唯一的亡故騎士。
I fear the lady may well have found her dead knight and it has brought her only grief.  Alas, alas, this life is but a vale of tears.	我恐怕那位夫人已經找到她亡故的騎士，卻只換來滿心悲痛。唉，唉，人生不過是一場淚水的谷地。
Little has changed, except for signs that your horse passed this way bearing Sir Gawaine back to Camelot.	此地大致如舊，唯有些痕跡顯示你的坐騎曾馱著高文爵士自此經過，返回肯萊特。
You have reached the heart of the forest where its dark power dwells.  It seems another unfortunate soul was here before you.	你已抵達森林深處，這股黑暗力量的所在。看來在你之前，還有另一個不幸的靈魂曾到過此地。
Only his bare bones remain, rattling in their shell of iron.	只剩下光禿禿的骸骨，在鐵甲的軀殼裡喀啦作響。
There is a piece of brightly colored silk tucked inside the armour.	盔甲裡塞著一片色彩鮮豔的絲巾。
There is nothing to gain by that.	這麼做並無所得。
He is the evil power that makes this forest so perilous.	他正是讓這座森林如此凶險的邪惡力量。
Once it was fine metal, now it is rusted and useless.	它曾是精良的金屬，如今已鏽蝕不堪，毫無用處。
The piece of silk was a lady's sleeve, a token to wear into battle.  We can only wonder what sad story was his, what favour he sought to win, and the sorrowful fate of the lady that may have awaited him with fading hope.	這片絲巾是一位夫人的衣袖，是他佩戴上戰場的信物。我們只能猜想，他有著怎樣悲傷的故事、渴望贏得誰的青睞，還有那位懷抱漸漸消逝的希望等待著他的夫人，又遭逢了何等悲涼的命運。
You cannot see what is not there.	不存在的東西，你看不見。
They are of the species Amanita Muscaria, a very dangerous mushroom at the best of times, said to cause madness or death.	它們屬於毒蠅傘一類，即便在最尋常的情況下也極為危險，據說會致人瘋狂或死亡。
But here in the Forest Perilous, they are doubly dangerous.  For if you so much as touch these mushrooms, you will be compelled to eat them.	但在派瑞樂斯森林裡，它們危險加倍——只要你一碰觸這些蕈菇，便會身不由己地把它們吃下肚。
There are no flowers nearby--only mushrooms.	附近沒有花，只有蕈菇。
It cannot be moved.	它無法被移動。
It juts from the heart of the forest like a jagged tooth.  There is evil power within it.	它從森林深處突出，宛如一顆參差的獠牙，其中蘊藏著邪惡的力量。
Most of the trees here are quite ordinary, but this one hoary, leafless tree may well be the eldest of them all.	這裡的樹大多平凡無奇，唯獨這株灰白、落盡了葉的老樹，很可能是其中最古老的一株。
It will be a grievous moment when Lady Elayne find the remains of her beloved knight.	當艾蓮公主找到她心愛騎士的遺骸時，那將是何等椎心之痛的一刻。
You already have a sleeve.	你已經有一條絲巾了。
You cannot get what is not there.	不存在的東西，你拿不到。
Odd.  Although this lady's sleeve has surely been here as long as the dead knight, it is as new as the day the lady wore it.  There is magick involved here.	奇怪。這條夫人的絲巾理應和亡故的騎士一同留在此地已久，卻新得彷彿夫人才剛佩戴過一般，其中必有魔法在作祟。
Your arms are not quite that long.	你的手臂沒有那麼長。
He said all he needed to say.  He will return nevermore.	他該說的話都已說完，不會再回來了。
Who dares to speak to Old Father Tree? You are but a twinkle in time, mortal.  Let me sleep the long and dreamless sleep of deep roots and sun on branch.	何人膽敢與老父樹交談？凡人啊，你不過是時光中一閃即逝的微光。且讓我沉入那深根與枝頭陽光交織的漫長無夢之眠吧。
Do not disturb him further, Arthur.  He is an old and weary tree.	別再驚擾他了，亞瑟。他是一株年邁而疲憊的樹。
That would not be much of a conversation.	那算不上什麼交談。
If you are greeting the dead knight, I fear he has long since ceased to care about such things.	你若是在向亡故的騎士問候，恐怕他早已不再在意這些事了。
They are dangerous.  Leave them be.	它們很危險，別去招惹。
I warn you most strongly, the merest touch of these mushrooms will compel you to eat them with the most dire results.	我要嚴正警告你，這些蕈菇哪怕只是輕輕一碰，都會逼得你把它們吃下肚，後果不堪設想。
There is no need to desecrate this poor dead knight.	沒有必要褻瀆這位可憐的亡故騎士。
Long has this unfortunate knight lain here, but you have not the time now to do him such a service.	這位不幸的騎士已在此長眠許久，但你此刻沒有時間為他做這件事。
This unfortunate knight is beyond your ability to help or hinder.	這位不幸的騎士，已非你的能力所能相助或妨礙。
The dead knight's armour is old and rusted and of no use to you.	亡故騎士的盔甲已老舊鏽蝕，對你毫無用處。
It would be futile to try.	嘗試也是徒勞。
He is gone, as I would hope you noticed.	他已經走了，我想你也該注意到了。
This stone would defy you.  You are well advised to leave it alone.	這塊石頭會與你對抗，你最好別去招惹它。
That is beyond your power or mine.	這已超出你我的能力範圍。
The knight has been dead far too long to be a threat to you.	這位騎士死去已久，早已構不成任何威脅。
Rawk!  I have no need for mortal toys.	呱！凡人的玩物，我用不著。
I doubt the dead knight has any interest in it.	我看那位亡故的騎士，對此不會有什麼興趣。
He is long past help, Arthur.	他早已無法可救了，亞瑟。
Rarawk!  Try it if you dare.  You will never touch me.	呱啦！有膽你就試試看，你永遠碰不到我。
The creature deserves it, but is not here for the attempt.	這畜生是罪有應得，只是牠此刻並不在此，由不得你動手。
O Fool, you seek death by coming here.  Turn back now or die!	愚者啊，你來到此地，便是自尋死路。速速回頭，否則便是一死！
Hear me, then, O Brave Fool.  The Black Knight is the greatest of all knights.  None have beaten him.  He is invincible.  Even Sir Gawaine was grievously wounded.	那便聽好了，勇敢的愚者。黑武士是天下第一的騎士，從無人能勝過他，他所向無敵。就連高文爵士也被他重創。
The Black Knight awaits you for a joust to the death.  Do you accept the challenge?	黑武士正等著與你來一場生死決鬥。你可願接受挑戰？
Then you must turn back, for you cannot pass this way through the forest without facing the Black Knight.	那你便得回頭，因為不與黑武士一戰，你休想從這條路穿越森林。
Crawk!  I shall delight in feeding on your bones when the Black Knight has finished with you!  I shall pluck out your eyes and peck at your bloody heart!	嘎呱！待黑武士收拾了你，我便能歡歡喜喜地啃食你的骨頭！我要啄出你的雙眼，啄食你血淋淋的心臟！
I have no time to waste on fools.  Turn back now or face him and die.	我沒空浪費在愚者身上，快回頭，否則便去見他，一死了之。
Would I tell such a fool as you even if I knew?	就算我知道，我又何必告訴你這樣的愚人？
He is a prisoner of the Black Knight and dies slowly of the wounds he received.	他是黑武士的階下囚，正因所受的傷勢緩緩步向死亡。
